/ by[c;f;t] groups table t by column(s) named by c, using function f for
/ computing results. Depending on f's rank, it is passed different arguments:
/   1) f[x] where x is a table of grouped columns;
/   2) f[x;y] where x is the original table t, and y is a constant function
/      returning grouping indices;
/   3) f[x;y;z] where x is the original table t, y is a constant function
/      returning grouping indices, and z the table with the grouping columns.
/ In the first two cases, if the result is a dict with generic values, it is
/ merged after the table with the grouping columns.
by:{[c;f;t]n:%?["A"~@k:t c;(1+|/'n)/n:%'k;k]
  m:{?[and["d"~@x;"A"~@.x];p.t[&¿p.n;p.c],x;x]}
  ?[1~r:rt.rank f; m f[:[;n]='t[;({0}^c)^!t]]
    2~r;           m f[t;:[;n]]
                   f[t;:[;n];t[&¿n;c]]]}
/ ij[c;t1;t2] returns the inner join of tables t1 and t2, using column(s) named
/ by c. If t1 c contains duplicates, only first match is used. It gives t2
/ priority for any other common columns.
ij:{[c;t1;t2](k;l):?[1<#c; (0,#*k)_%(1+|/'n)/n:%'(k:t1 c),'t2 c; (t1 c:*c;t2 c)]
  i:k?l; t1[i@j],t2[j:&i<#k;({1}#c)^!t2]}
/ join is a more general variant of ij that handles duplicate entries in t1 c.
/ Implementation is based on code shared by @Marshall on the matrix chat.
join:{[c;t1;t2]
  (i;j):?[1<#c; (0,#*k)_%(1+|/'n)/n:%'(k:t1 c),'t2 c; (0,#k)_%(k:t1 c),t2 c:*c]
  t1[&(=j)i],t2@,/(=(!#j)!j)i}
/ oj[c;t1;t2] returns the outer join of tables t1 and t2 using column(s) named
/ by c. If t1 c contains duplicates, only first match is used. It gives t2
/ priority for any other common columns and uses ""/0i/0n for missing fields in
/ t1.
oj:{[c;t1;t2](k;l):?[1<#c; (0,#*k)_%(1+|/'n)/n:%'(k:t1 c),'t2 c; (t1 c:*c;t2 c)]
  j:&(#k)=i:k?l; fij:{[i;j|x]j or:x@i; @[x@i;j;:;?["I"~t:@x;0i;"N"~t;0n;*0#x]]}
  (fij't1),t2}
/ flip[t] returns a transposed table where column names are given by the first
/ column, or column "key" if it exists (inspired by Lil's flip primitive).
flip:{[t]("key"¿1_!t)and t:t[;"key",("key"=)^!t]; ..[key:1_!t],{(*'x)!1_'x}@+.t}
1
